From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bundle the LICENSE into the wheel

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted yet: a general packaging gap affecting every platform's wheel, not riscv64-specific, but filing it needs separate upstream coordination]

python/scripts/create_wheel.sh assembles the wheel's dist-info by hand
(METADATA/WHEEL/entry_points.txt/RECORD) and never copies LICENSE into
it, even though pyproject.toml declares license = {file = "LICENSE"}.
The real published pyscn/pyscn-mcp wheels on PyPI have the same gap
(verified against pyscn-1.33.1-py3-none-manylinux_2_34_x86_64.whl).
RISE distributes the riscv64 wheel this port builds, so licence
compliance for it is ours regardless of upstream's own gap.

Copy LICENSE into <pkg>-<version>.dist-info/licenses/LICENSE when
present, which RECORD's generic `find . -type f` walk picks up
automatically. No other platform's build is affected.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 python/scripts/create_wheel.sh | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/python/scripts/create_wheel.sh b/python/scripts/create_wheel.sh
index 3e4d7ca..dc58b5c 100755
--- a/python/scripts/create_wheel.sh
+++ b/python/scripts/create_wheel.sh
@@ -262,6 +262,14 @@ create_wheel() {
     for binary_path in "${binary_paths[@]}"; do
         cp "$binary_path" "$bin_dir/"
     done
+
+    # create_wheel.sh ships no LICENSE in dist-info (neither does the real
+    # published pyscn/pyscn-mcp wheel), even though pyproject.toml declares
+    # one; bundle it so the wheels this repo distributes carry it.
+    if [[ -f "$project_dir/LICENSE" ]]; then
+        mkdir -p "$metadata_dir/licenses"
+        cp "$project_dir/LICENSE" "$metadata_dir/licenses/LICENSE"
+    fi
     
     # Check if README exists
     if [[ ! -f "$readme_path" ]]; then
--
